{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>If I have sharpened.</b> Past tense in place of future, as is the way of prophecies, and the meaning is 'if I sharpen, I shall render vengeance,' and it is not an expression of doubt but a promise and language of certainty. And the sense of the verse is: I shall sharpen My sword in heaven above, and let My hand grasp judgment below — and it is the word of the prophet (Isaiah 34:5): ״כי רותה בשמים חרבי הנה על אדום תרד״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'If I have sharpened the lightning of My sword' — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: If I sharpen My sword, with the lightning of My sword I destroy the world, and what shall I do? 'And let My hand grasp' — thus far. <br><b>And you should know that</b> the sword of the Holy One, blessed be He, mentioned in every place, is His attribute of judgment, as it says (Isaiah 66:16) ״ובחרבו את כל בשר״, (Psalms 22:21) ״הצילה מחרב נפשי״, and similar verses; and it is fitting for a person to be frightened and to recoil from before it, as the verse says fully (Job 19:29) ״גורו לכם מפני חרב״, which means: you sons of men, you should fear the sword above, for sins cause pestilence and the sword below, and for this reason you should know that there is judgment and the world is not random. And I have already written on the verse (Genesis 3:24) ״להט החרב״, and on the verse (Deuteronomy 7:24) ״לא יתיצב איש״, that the harsh sword of the Holy One, blessed be He, has 16 faces, and that which He mentions here ״חרבי״ and immediately adjacent to it ״ותאחז״ is to allude to חרב י״ו (the sword of sixteen). The wicked are judged by it and the righteous are frightened by it, but it is delivered into their hand; and this is what you find in the new song for the future (Psalms 149:6) ״רוממות אל בגרונם וחרב פיפיות בידם״ — read in it י״ו פיות (sixteen mouths), and this is clear." "<b>Behold,</b> this poem is a great consolation and a clear promise regarding the redemption and the destruction of idolaters and the vengeance of Israel against their enemies and the atonement of Israel for their sins. And perhaps because of this the sign of the breaks came to our Rabbis, of blessed memory — זי״ו ל״ך — ordained by Ezra the Scribe, the priest, the prophet, who saw by the Holy Spirit that his ordinance regarding the public reading of the Torah scroll would be an enduring ordinance in every generation, never to be annulled at any time. And he established this sign in the breaks of this parashah, accepted among us, to signify that the זיו (radiance) and the זוהר (brilliance) and the כבוד (glory) and the תפארת (splendor) will return to Israel as at first, and ״שבו בנים לגבולם״." "<b>I shall render vengeance to My adversaries.</b> That is, I shall render them recompense as they did to Israel, and the Holy One, blessed be He, called them His adversaries; and above He mentioned ״פן ינכרו צרימו״, whereas to Israel the designation returns — and the verse teaches you that the adversaries of Israel are the adversaries of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>And so</b> you find in the Egyptian exile, in the Song of the Sea (Exodus 15:7): ״תהרוס קמיך״ — when it should have said ״קמינו״; but the verse teaches that those who rise against us are as if they rise against Him, may He be exalted. And this is what David, of blessed memory, said (Psalms 83): ״כי הנה אויביך יהמיון ומשנאיך נשאו ראש, על עמך יערימו סוד ויתיעצו על צפוניך״ — He called the nations His enemies and His haters, may He be blessed, when they scheme and plot against Israel, whom He called ״צפוניך״, on account of their being hidden with Him and under His hand, in the manner of (Exodus 19:5) ״והייתם לי סגולה״, for the סגולה is not assigned a deputy or governor over it by the king, but is hidden with him and under his hand. Or He called them צפונים on account of their being the sole inheritors of גן עדן and the abundant good that is hidden (צפון)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya cites Isaiah 34:5 but writes only '(שם לד)', i.e., 'there 34'; the preceding prooftext was Isaiah 66, so 'there' means in Isaiah. Normalized to Isaiah 34:5."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:47.257847144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}